  "description": "KILHUK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C176 H158 N22 O22 Yb6,C2 H6 O1,3(C1 H4 O1),5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 5 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 4 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 5 O neighbors; Yb4 (Yb) has 5 O neighbors; Yb5 (Yb) has 4 O neighbors; Yb6 (Yb) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a chain with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.743-3.744 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 107.67-110.72°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C181H180N22O31Yb6.",
